            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0410" n="298" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg298"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2784/1.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Morgan to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-11-26"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 26, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 279.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose, in duplicate,
                    an extract from the Official Gazette of the 23d instant, which contained decree
                    No. 158 of the provisional governor, relative to the collection of evidence and
                    the settlement of claims arising against the Government of Cuba by reason of the
                    recent insurrection in this island.</p>
                <p>Although the personnel of the claims commission has not been announced, it is
                    understood that it will be composed of two officers of the army of pacification
                    and one judge of the audiencia of Habana. The American members will probably be
                    Maj. Francis J. Kernan and Capt. George W. Read, of the general staff, and the
                    Cuban official judge, Manuel Landa y Gonzalez.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin V. Morgan.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d257-a1.xml" xpointer="d257-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
